{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99914","id":2209519918,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Dspku","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99914","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99914.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99914.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99914","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99914/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99914/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99914/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e5030f3e09ec17a467e44b8ed37b18abc44c687a","number":99914,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"On bad array access error, bubble up the error","user":{"login":"alecmeyer","id":113138392,"node_id":"U_kgDOBr5a2A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113138392?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer","html_url":"https://github.com/alecmeyer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecmeyer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Addresses issue #98519 \"Importing a large 400mb gltf/glb file crashes at 99%\"\r\n\r\nI would like to correct something incorrect that I said in a previous comment. I erroneously said before that upon importing the corrupt glb file to a new Godot project for the first time, it would remain unresponsive indefinitely. This was not actually the case. In truth, Godot only remains responsive for a very long time (about 10 minutes on my machine) but it will eventually arrive at the bad unsigned integer square brackets operation that I described, whether on the first try or any succeeding tries.\r\n\r\nMy fix does resolve the crashing for this case. It eventually returns Godot to a responsive state (as opposed to being unresponsive indefinitely), and communicates the error via notifications and on the console. It notably does NOT revert the state of the project to prior to the corrupt import.\r\n\r\nAfter the exception is caught:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc7c2232-59a0-47f2-aa45-d2da83013391)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6c7791e-1c8b-4df4-a8db-3efb2f15ef76)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f644a55e-92a0-4412-b38b-bbdde01eec63)\r\n\r\nI believe the red X icon in the FileSystem correctly indicates that the file is corrupt, which is nice.\r\nAdditionally, I am under the impression that throwing an exception from the STD library is unconventional in the codebase but I am not familiar with the desirable standard.\r\n\r\nI would be very pleased to make whatever modifications are seen fit.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":311852125,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzM